00:39:20.610 --> 00:39:22.409
know, but the way things ended up

00:39:22.410 --> 00:39:24.539
shaking out government got better

00:39:24.540 --> 00:39:25.439
at what it was doing.

00:39:25.440 --> 00:39:27.329
It stopped doing certain things.

00:39:27.330 --> 00:39:28.229
They balanced the budget.

00:39:28.230 --> 00:39:30.419
Yeah. And, you know, and we

00:39:30.420 --> 00:39:32.249
actually, you know, government

00:39:32.250 --> 00:39:33.719
the size, scope and spending of

00:39:33.720 --> 00:39:35.309
government, relatively speaking,

00:39:35.310 --> 00:39:36.929
declined.

00:39:36.930 --> 00:39:38.849
And then under Bush,

00:39:38.850 --> 00:39:40.169
when government started doing a lot

00:39:40.170 --> 00:39:41.609
of different things and it was not

00:39:41.610 --> 00:39:43.349
going well whether it was in the

00:39:43.350 --> 00:39:44.999
economy or wars and things like

00:39:45.000 --> 00:39:46.019
that, government grew.

00:39:46.020 --> 00:39:48.299
So it's an interesting

00:39:48.300 --> 00:39:50.399
I mean, I take some flak

00:39:50.400 --> 00:39:51.569
for this and I you know, I

00:39:51.570 --> 00:39:53.159
